  "id": "preview-kickoff-right",
  "title": "PREVIEW — Right kickoff: watch, then learn",
  "description": "Watch a smooth right-side kickoff break: 7 drives the flank, 9 stays central, 11 arrives late at the far post, and 2 and 10 support behind the ball.",
  "tags": [
    "preview",
    "kickoff",
    "8v8",
    "right",
    "teaching replay"
  ],
  "notes": "FIRST PASS: Watch the kickoff flow without teaching overlays. The striker lays the ball back, the CAM releases RM #7 early, and every supporting player keeps moving at a steady pace.\n\nSECOND PASS: RM #7 stays in the right channel and drives toward the end line. ST #9 runs straight through the centre lane and finishes between the posts. LM #11 stays wide on the far side for longer, then makes a late diagonal run inside the far post.\n\nFINAL DECISION: RD #2 closes to a useful supporting distance behind 7, while CAM #10 remains available for the inside cutback. From the final picture, 7 can recycle to 2, cut back to 10, or cross to 9 or 11. GK #1 advances toward the edge of the home penalty area as the team moves up.\n\nSETUP: Attack left to right on the 60 × 40 m 8v8 pitch. The right side is the bottom touchline. Pair this drill with the mirrored left-side kickoff.",
